  m_Name: ScrollCompressorData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Scroll Compressor
  engineDescription: A Scroll Compressor is a positive-displacement compressor used
    for compressing gases and refrigerants by using two interleaving spiral-shaped
    scrolls, one stationary and one orbiting. Its main components include the fixed
    scroll, orbiting scroll, crankshaft or eccentric drive, motor, casing, suction
    port, discharge port, bearings, and sealing elements. During operation, the orbiting
    scroll moves in an orbital path around the fixed scroll without rotating about
    its own axis. This movement creates enclosed pockets of gas between the two scrolls.
    Gas enters through the outer region of the scrolls, and as the orbiting motion
    continues, the trapped gas pockets move toward the center while their volume
    decreases. The compressed gas is finally discharged through the central outlet.
    Scroll compressors are widely used in refrigeration systems, air-conditioning
    units, heat pumps, automotive air-conditioning systems, and compact industrial
    equipment. From an engineering perspective, understanding scroll geometry, orbital
    motion, compression efficiency, leakage, sealing, lubrication, thermal behavior,
    vibration, and wear characteristics is essential for achieving quiet, efficient,
    and reliable operation.
  engineCategory: Engineering
